.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DEVFS_HOTPLUG 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm devfs_hotplug
.Nd publish and withdraw device-model nodes in devfs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.In vfs/vfs.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_publish "struct device *dev" "struct fs_node *node" "const char *path"
.Ft void
.Fn device_unpublish "struct device *dev"
.Ft void
.Fn devfs_register_device "struct fs_node *node"
.Ft void
.Fn devfs_unregister_device "struct fs_node *node"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The device model may associate a backing devfs node with a
.Vt struct device
by calling
.Fn device_publish .
Once the device is registered with a bus, the framework publishes the node into
.Xr devfs 5
at the supplied relative path.
.Pp
When the device is unregistered,
.Fn device_unpublish
and
.Fn devfs_unregister_device
remove the exported node and any framework-managed aliases.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devfs_naming 9 ,
.Xr devfs_permissions 9 ,
.Xr device_register 9
